# K9 - Fitness functions before architecture claims. Kata sandbox sketch (plan section 3.6).
# [K9-nn] sketch IDs are recognised by validate_architecture / trace and ignored by the
# CI adl-coverage gate. Never [TR-*]; promotion is decided only at K12 (architecture/REVIEW.md).
DESCRIPTION K9 - what the ADL promises, what CI enforces, and what is declared unmeasured
CATEGORY Architectural Capabilities
NAMESPACE TrK9NS
DEFINE SYSTEM Total Recall K9 Sandbox AS trk9
    DEFINE COMPONENT Performance Targets AS targets
    DEFINE COMPONENT CI Claims AS ciclaims
    DEFINE COMPONENT Unmeasured Claims AS unmeasured

# Course pp. 52-53, 64-65: a capability is only real once a fitness function measures it. capabilities.adl
# states the performance targets in prose (1000 writes/s, recall p95 under 150 ms, 20000 memories) and
# scripts/loadtest-budget.json is what the benchmark fails on. If the two drift the ADL promises more than
# anything checks. Memories are per vault: the loadtest fills two, so lt_n x 2.
ASSERT(Performance Targets: the writes per second, recall p95 and memory count stated in capabilities.adl equal the full profile of loadtest-budget.json) # [K9-01]

# A comment that says a target is "not in CI" is a claim about the gate. mutation.yml runs the benchmark
# against the budget (smoke in the PR gate, full weekly), so the comment understates the enforcement.
ASSERT(CI Claims: what capabilities.adl says about CI enforcement matches the workflows) # [K9-02]

# The README says retrieval quality is "not yet measured". That is honest only if the gap has a backlog
# entry with a trigger, so it has a way to end (GOVERNANCE section 3).
ASSERT(Unmeasured Claims: every "not yet measured" claim in the README has a backlog entry with a trigger) # [K9-03]

# Not re-asserted, answered with existing evidence (answers.md): the spec-driven eval (scripts/eval/spec-eval.ts
# and its CI test), the budget in the PR gate, the ADL coverage gate (TR-Q-series).
